{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_desktop", "label": "The menu bar app (docs/desktop.md)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/desktop.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_desktop_tauri_app", "label": "Tauri menu bar app drives the CLI", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/desktop.md", "source_location": "intro", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An interface rather than a second implementation: everything it knows about Parlour it learns by running the CLI, and every setting it writes goes through parlour config write, so the app and the terminal can never disagree about the same house. It does not bundle Node or the package because one copy of Parlour is better than two that can disagree."}, {"id": "docs_desktop_supervisor", "label": "supervisor.rs (parlour start --events child)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/desktop.md", "source_location": "## How it fits together", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stopping sends SIGINT rather than SIGKILL, because Parlour shuts ffmpeg down on it and an orphaned ffmpeg would keep hold of the microphone."}, {"id": "docs_desktop_bridge", "label": "lib/bridge.ts, the only caller of invoke()", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/desktop.md", "source_location": "## How it fits together", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_desktop_generic_parlour_command", "label": "main.rs generic parlour(args, stdin) command", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/desktop.md", "source_location": "## How it fits together", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The Rust side knows the path to the parlour binary and nothing else; config, secrets, doctor and connectors all go through the CLI's --json and stdin interfaces."}, {"id": "docs_desktop_settings_json", "label": "App settings.json (parlourBin, autostart)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/desktop.md", "source_location": "## How it fits together", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The app's only two facts. The path is kept as long as it is executable so the app will not swap a checkout's parlour-dev back for the global copy."}, {"id": "docs_desktop_onboarding", "label": "Onboarding (find/install parlour, init --porcelain, questions, doctor)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/desktop.md", "source_location": "## The tabs", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_desktop_parlour_dev", "label": "bin/parlour-dev for running the CLI from source", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/desktop.md", "source_location": "## Running the app against a checkout", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_desktop_app_vs_launchagent", "label": "App and LaunchAgent are alternatives, not a pair", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/desktop.md", "source_location": "## Two things worth knowing", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two copies of Parlour means two processes fighting over one microphone and one port, so parlour init sets up only one and the app leaves the agent to itself."}, {"id": "docs_desktop_microphone_permission", "label": "Microphone permission belongs to whatever starts it", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/desktop.md", "source_location": "## Two things worth knowing", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "macOS grants the mic to the responsible process, which for anything the app spawns is the app. Onboarding opens the device briefly to trigger the prompt; the bundle carries NSMicrophoneUsageDescription or macOS refuses rather than asks. A LaunchAgent is a separate grant."}, {"id": "docs_desktop_no_tauri_plugins", "label": "No Tauri plugins, capability list core:default", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/desktop.md", "source_location": "## Deliberate choices", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Everything the app does happens in Rust where it can be reasoned about. Activation policy Accessory: no Dock icon, tray is the way back, closing the window leaves Parlour running."}, {"id": "docs_desktop_generated_icons", "label": "Icons generated from src-tauri/icon.png", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/desktop.md", "source_location": "## Deliberate choices", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only icon.png is in git; the source sits outside icons/ because tauri icon writes an icon.png into its output and a source kept there would rewrite itself on every build."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_desktop", "target": "docs_architecture_events_stream", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/desktop.md", "source_location": "## How it fits together", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_desktop_tauri_app", "target": "docs_desktop_generic_parlour_command", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/desktop.md", "source_location": "## How it fits together", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_desktop_tauri_app", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_09_16_parlour_extraction_design_cli_surface", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/desktop.md", "source_location": "## The tabs", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_desktop_bridge", "target": "docs_desktop_generic_parlour_command", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score